From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gigi <42325924+g-cqd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:16:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Web Extensions: blocking webRequest.onHeadersReceived
 listeners (Sunset W6c)

The network process asks the UI process before handing a response on,
for pages whose extensions have a blocking onHeadersReceived listener
(registered as WebRequestOnHeadersReceivedBlocking). The UI process asks
those listeners through WebExtensionWebRequestDecision (now answering
either a request or response headers) under the same 2 s limit. The web
process reads { cancel } and { responseHeaders } (value or binaryValue),
given or promised, and does not call those listeners again for the
same response.

A cancelled response fails as blocked by a content blocker. A response
whose headers were changed is not stored in the HTTP cache, since a
load from the cache is not asked. Not asked: synchronous loads,
multipart responses, and 304 revalidations.

Also: the onBeforeRequest message was encoded after its reply handler
had moved the request out (a message holds references to its
arguments); both messages are now given copies.

ResourceResponseBase::setHTTPHeaderFields is exported for WebKit.

